{"type":"document","version":"0.5","doc":"fmjl_rulebook","source":"fmjl_rulebook_v0.5.md","sha256":"5ee0924735999d929b8dc3ebbd9beef204cb4ed289967aac85b6e5cef1f359bc","protection":"none","signed":false,"converter":"fmjl 0.5","structure":true,"elements":124,"created":"2026-09-29T12:08:51Z","lang":"en","access":["all"],"title":"FMJL Rulebook, Version 0.5","authors":["Rupak Kumar"],"summary":"The rules of FMJL: one document, two forms - .fmjl storage for machines and Markdown authoring for people.","last_id":124}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","hash":"26016c96236cf40e","type":"heading","level":1,"parent":null,"characters":28,"md":"# FMJL Rulebook, Version 0.5"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e2","hash":"d80c35e662310bd9","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":51,"md":"Status: draft. License: MIT, copyright Rupak Kumar."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e3","hash":"92017458924c0166","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":187,"md":"This rulebook is the authority for FMJL. The `fmjl` tool, the Python package of the same name, is the reference implementation: if the tool and this rulebook disagree, the tool has a bug."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e4","hash":"3f9d59778e29dae4","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":18,"md":"## 1. What FMJL Is"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e5","hash":"f4b0a4194169fdc7","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e4","characters":226,"md":"FMJL stores any document as a list of small parts called elements, such as headings, paragraphs, tables, and images. It is built so that people can read and write documents easily, and machines can search and use them quickly."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e6","hash":"8f072e1685488653","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e4","characters":29,"md":"FMJL combines four languages:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e7","hash":"675a8db6180a13c4","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e4","characters":329,"md":"| Language | Role | Where it appears |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| JSON (JSON Lines) | The container of the storage form | Every line of an `.fmjl` file |\n| Markdown | All readable text | The `md` field, and the whole authoring form |\n| LaTeX | Math formulas | The `latex` field |\n| HTML | Tables with merged cells | The `html` field |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e8","hash":"d3f4b2259a34558f","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e4","characters":38,"md":"Three rules make sure nothing is lost:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e9","hash":"d4fd800be283deda","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e4","characters":304,"md":"1. Every part of the original document becomes an element, including stamps, logos, watermarks, and blacked-out areas.\n2. Every element from a page-based file records its page and position, so its exact spot in the original can always be found.\n3. The original file is always kept next to the FMJL files."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e10","hash":"3f4879d46b1aab66","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":29,"md":"## 2. One Document, Two Forms"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e11","hash":"110a78afff7163c5","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e10","characters":87,"md":"Every FMJL document can be written in two forms that hold exactly the same information:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e12","hash":"9b85b1a8cc1659ef","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e10","characters":356,"md":"|  | Storage form | Authoring form |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| File | `name.fmjl` | `name.md` |\n| Looks like | One JSON object per line | Normal Markdown, with small hidden notes |\n| Made for | Machines: search, RAG, databases | People: reading, writing, reviewing |\n| Opens in | Any JSON Lines tool or language | Any Markdown editor, GitHub, VS Code preview |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e13","hash":"c65525542f91a4e1","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e10","characters":208,"md":"The tool converts between the two forms without losing anything: `fmjl new` turns the authoring form into the storage form, and `fmjl md` turns it back. Converting there and back always gives the same result."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e14","hash":"24cb364fb8323816","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e10","characters":16,"md":"Recommended use:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e15","hash":"ebd16f6bc586d0ef","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e10","characters":188,"md":"1. People write and edit the authoring form.\n2. Machines read the storage form.\n3. Version control (such as Git) keeps the authoring form, because its short lines make changes easy to see."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e16","hash":"0a6e10d61d720a46","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":20,"md":"## 3. Storage Layout"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e17","hash":"465c13b2d1101a2a","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e16","characters":56,"md":"While processing, each document is stored as one folder:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e18","hash":"1b6832f52737c9d9","type":"code","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e16","characters":211,"md":"```text\nleave_policy/\n  leave_policy.fmjl     the storage form\n  leave_policy.md       the authoring form (optional)\n  images/               cropped images\n  original/             the untouched original file\n```"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e19","hash":"bed734740a4238b7","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e16","characters":57,"md":"For sharing, the same folder is packed into one zip file."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e20","hash":"10a7ac5f29805333","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e16","characters":128,"md":"The name FMJL is short for Format, Markdown, JSON Lines, and it is also the file extension, `.fmjl`. Rules for the storage form:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e21","hash":"c5ee3df4fa7d7d6f","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e16","characters":246,"md":"1. Text encoding is UTF-8.\n2. Each line is exactly one JSON object. Lines end with a newline character, and there are no empty lines.\n3. Line 1 is the header line. Every following line is an element line.\n4. Element lines appear in reading order."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e22","hash":"55e0bab07574ae16","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e16","characters":174,"md":"Lines in the storage form can be very long, because a whole table is one line. To compare two versions, use the authoring form, or `git diff --word-diff` on the storage form."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e23","hash":"46222849367e7a5b","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":21,"md":"## 4. The Header Line"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e24","hash":"3575c1e071b220f0","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e23","characters":103,"md":"The header line describes the whole document. It has `\"type\": \"document\"` and these 12 required fields:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e25","hash":"c4cec095d1e494bb","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e23","characters":1135,"md":"| Field | Value | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `version` | Text | The rulebook version the file follows, for example `\"0.5\"` |\n| `doc` | Text | Short document name, using lowercase letters, digits, `_` or `-` |\n| `source` | Text | The original file name |\n| `sha256` | 64 hexadecimal characters | Fingerprint of the original file, used to skip duplicate uploads |\n| `protection` | `none`, `password`, `certificate`, or `drm` | How the original file was locked |\n| `signed` | `true` or `false` | Whether the original carries a digital signature |\n| `converter` | Text | The tool and version that created this file |\n| `structure` | `true` or `false` | `false` means no headings were found, so the file should be converted again with a better tool |\n| `elements` | Whole number, or `null` | The number of element lines; `null` only while the file is still being written |\n| `created` | Date and time (ISO 8601, UTC) | When the file was created |\n| `lang` | Language code | The main language, for example `\"en\"`, `\"hi\"`, `\"as\"`, or `\"bn\"` |\n| `access` | List of group names | The default permission, for example `[\"all\"]` or `[\"hr\"]` |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e26","hash":"fd79d371cf13390f","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e23","characters":52,"md":"Optional header fields describe the document itself:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e27","hash":"9c136bd448b1a895","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e23","characters":464,"md":"| Field | Value | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `title` | Text | The document's title |\n| `authors` | List of names | Who wrote the document |\n| `date` | `YYYY`, `YYYY-MM`, or `YYYY-MM-DD` | The document's own date, not the conversion date |\n| `summary` | Text | A short summary of the whole document |\n| `last_id` | Whole number | The highest element number ever given, so numbers are never reused (section 7.1) |\n| `meta` | Object | Custom data (section 7.6) |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e28","hash":"a20fcd3f0c58864f","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e23","characters":115,"md":"Security rule: `protection` records only how a file was locked. A password or key is never stored anywhere in FMJL."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e29","hash":"2a72f743262f5baa","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":19,"md":"## 5. Element Lines"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e30","hash":"1aa7e9aba1c47710","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e29","characters":23,"md":"### 5.1 Required Fields"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e31","hash":"072a0f5abef830aa","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e30","characters":38,"md":"Every element line has these 6 fields:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e32","hash":"c11a5e865114b518","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e30","characters":505,"md":"| Field | Value | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `id` | Text | `<doc>#e<number>`, for example `leave_policy#e7` (section 7.1) |\n| `hash` | 16 hexadecimal characters | Content fingerprint (section 7.2) |\n| `type` | One of the 20 types | What kind of part this is (section 6) |\n| `parent` | Element ID or `null` | The heading or group this element belongs to (section 7.4) |\n| `characters` | Whole number | The number of characters in `md` |\n| `md` | Text | The content, in canonical Markdown (section 8) |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e33","hash":"a17cda2f0b8f1b73","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e29","characters":23,"md":"### 5.2 Optional Fields"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e34","hash":"128e8677c8467ef3","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e33","characters":1180,"md":"| Field | Value | Used when |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `subtype` | Text | The element is an `image`, `noise`, or `group` |\n| `label` | Lowercase name, for example `inputs` | People want to refer to the element by name |\n| `level` | 1 to 6 | The element is a `heading` (required for headings) |\n| `page` | Whole number, from 0 | The element sits on one page |\n| `pages` | List of page numbers | The element spans several pages |\n| `bbox` | `[left, top, right, bottom]` | The position on the page is known |\n| `reference` | Element ID, or a list of two or more IDs | The element points to other elements |\n| `continues` | Element ID | The element is the next part of a split element |\n| `confidence` | Number from 0 to 1 | The content came from OCR or an AI model |\n| `lang` | Language code | The element's language differs from the header |\n| `access` | List of group names | The element's permission differs from the header |\n| `html` | Text | A `table` has merged cells or multi-level headers |\n| `latex` | Text | The element is a `formula` (required for formulas) |\n| `file` | Path | The element is an `image` (required for images) |\n| `meta` | Object | Custom data (section 7.6) |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e35","hash":"6d181716592a4cc8","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e33","characters":154,"md":"When an optional field is missing, a default applies: no `confidence` means fully certain (1), and no `lang` or `access` means the header's value applies."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e36","hash":"32a3c306753f9b78","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":19,"md":"## 6. Element Types"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e37","hash":"6f604d17397e7138","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e36","characters":1815,"md":"| # | Type | Holds | Rules |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | `heading` | Titles and subtitles | Needs `level` |\n| 2 | `paragraph` | Normal text | Inline math uses `$...$` (section 8) |\n| 3 | `list` | Bullet or numbered points | A whole list is one element |\n| 4 | `table` | Rows and columns | May add `html`; long tables may be split (section 11) |\n| 5 | `formula` | Display math | Needs `latex`; `md` is `$$` + `latex` + `$$` |\n| 6 | `code` | Program code | `md` is a fenced code block that names the language |\n| 7 | `image` | Pictures, charts, logos, stamps, signatures, QR codes | Needs `file`; `md` holds a text description |\n| 8 | `caption` | The label of a table or image | `reference` points to that table or image |\n| 9 | `footnote` | Notes at the bottom of a page | `md` starts with `[^n]: `; `reference` points to the text that carries `[^n]` |\n| 10 | `form_field` | Form entries and checkboxes | `md` looks like `- [x] Married` |\n| 11 | `annotation` | Comments and handwritten notes | Usually has `confidence` |\n| 12 | `redaction` | Blacked-out hidden parts | `md` is `[REDACTED]` |\n| 13 | `noise` | Page headers, footers, watermarks, page numbers | Needs `subtype` |\n| 14 | `message` | One email or chat message | Sender and date go at the top of `md` |\n| 15 | `utterance` | One speaker's turn in a transcript | Speaker and time go at the top of `md` |\n| 16 | `record` | One CSV row or one JSON object | `md` lists the fields as `Name: value` |\n| 17 | `citation` | A reference or bibliography entry | In-text markers link here with `reference` |\n| 18 | `quote` | Quoted text from another source | `md` uses `>` |\n| 19 | `toc` | A table of contents | Kept for structure |\n| 20 | `group` | A container, such as a slide, a sidebar, or a figure with several images | Needs `subtype`; `md` holds its title |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e38","hash":"cc154e12ad3504cd","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e36","characters":9,"md":"Subtypes:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e39","hash":"04dae2d5662f9738","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e36","characters":305,"md":"1. For `image`: `logo`, `stamp`, `signature`, `chart`, `diagram`, `photo`, `qr_code`, or `barcode`. For `qr_code` and `barcode`, `md` also holds the decoded value.\n2. For `noise`: `header`, `footer`, `watermark`, or `page_number`.\n3. For `group`: `slide`, `sidebar`, `figure`, `box`, `sheet`, or `thread`."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e40","hash":"644aa8b33599262d","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":17,"md":"## 7. Field Rules"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e41","hash":"2fa8e40cc8acf910","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e40","characters":11,"md":"### 7.1 IDs"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e42","hash":"e9085a5363f5e4b2","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e41","characters":336,"md":"1. An ID is `<doc>#e<number>` and is unique in the document.\n2. An ID never changes once given, even when other elements are added or removed.\n3. A new element gets the next free number, which is `last_id` plus 1. Numbers of removed elements are never reused.\n4. Reading order comes from the order of the lines, not from the ID numbers."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e43","hash":"b196bbbf8c7fe33e","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e40","characters":12,"md":"### 7.2 Hash"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e44","hash":"2a0499e914e51ce6","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e43","characters":211,"md":"`hash` is the first 16 hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 of the text `type`, a newline, then `md`, encoded in UTF-8. When a document is uploaded again, only elements whose `hash` changed need new embeddings."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e45","hash":"440d492dfc79dedc","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e43","characters":187,"md":"Hashes are only compared within one document, so 16 characters (64 bits) are enough. Even a document with 1 million elements has about a 1 in 37 million chance of any two hashes matching."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e46","hash":"06b08ada7311ba7e","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e40","characters":27,"md":"### 7.3 Pages and Positions"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e47","hash":"5c389e4a2d02c54b","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e46","characters":455,"md":"1. Page numbers start at 0. When showing a page number to users, add 1.\n2. An element has `page` or `pages`, never both. `pages` holds at least two numbers, in order.\n3. `bbox` is `[left, top, right, bottom]` in whole numbers from 0 to 1000, where 1000 is the full page width or height and `[0, 0]` is the top-left corner.\n4. `bbox` is allowed only together with `page`.\n5. For slides, `page` is the slide number. For spreadsheets, it is the sheet number."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e48","hash":"ca9d0379b50d1c6d","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e40","characters":26,"md":"### 7.4 Parents and Groups"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e49","hash":"e1dd5b2e0683ac21","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e48","characters":388,"md":"1. `parent` points to a `heading` or a `group` that comes earlier in the file.\n2. By default, an element's parent is the nearest heading above it with a lower level. Inside a group, the default parent is the group, or a heading inside that group.\n3. A heading's parent, when it is a heading, must have a smaller level.\n4. Groups can hold any elements, including headings and other groups."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e50","hash":"47d563b1d5d44455","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e40","characters":30,"md":"### 7.5 Links Between Elements"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e51","hash":"e6a05de20eb780f2","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e50","characters":611,"md":"1. `reference` links an element to others: a caption to its table, a footnote to its text, a chart image to the table holding its data.\n2. `continues` links the parts of a split element in order. Each part has the same type as the part before it.\n3. Inside `md`, a Markdown link can point to an element in the same document by ID or label: `[Table 1](#e7)` or `[Table 1](#inputs)`.\n4. A `label` is unique in the document and never changes the ID.\n5. A footnote marker inside `md` is `[^n]`, where `n` is the footnote's number in the source. The footnote element's `md` begins with `[^n]: ` followed by its text."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e52","hash":"14a0b3b24f6ae4e7","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e40","characters":19,"md":"### 7.6 Custom Data"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e53","hash":"f3a77e0dc9bdafcc","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e52","characters":424,"md":"`meta` holds custom data on the header or on any element. To avoid clashes, use names that start with your organization, such as `\"acme.department\"`. One name is reserved: `facts`, a list of extracted facts, for example `[{\"name\": \"fee\", \"value\": \"₹5,000\"}]`. Names that start with `fmjl.` are reserved for the tools; for example, an importer records the tracked changes it accepted as `fmjl.tracked_changes` (section 10.1)."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e54","hash":"f621f70b354582f6","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":24,"md":"## 8. Canonical Markdown"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e55","hash":"dce594dd3325404f","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e54","characters":221,"md":"The same content must always give the same `md` text, so that the same content always gives the same `hash`. `md` follows CommonMark plus GitHub-style tables, strikethrough, and task lists, written in this canonical form:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e56","hash":"56370a6e3a71c656","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e54","characters":1098,"md":"1. Lines end with a newline character only, with no spaces at the end of a line.\n2. A hard line break is written as a backslash at the end of the line.\n3. Headings use `#` marks followed by one space, for example `## Annual Leave`.\n4. Bullet list markers are `-`.\n5. Tables are written as `| cell | cell |`, with separator cells `---`, `:---`, `---:`, or `:---:`.\n6. A `table` with `html`: the HTML is the exact structure, and `md` is made from it by repeating each merged cell in every cell it covers. HTML written by a tool is in canonical form: `<table>` and `</table>` on their own lines, one `<tr>` per line, `th` cells in the first row and `td` cells below, `rowspan` before `colspan`, only `&amp;`, `&lt;` and `&gt;` as entities, and no other tags or attributes.\n7. A `formula`: `latex` is the formula, and `md` is `$$` + `latex` + `$$`.\n8. Inline math is written between single dollar signs. A dollar sign followed by a digit is always money, never math, so \"$50\" is always an amount. A literal dollar sign can also be written as `\\$`.\n9. `code` elements keep their text exactly as written."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e57","hash":"6db1c8f0b41d89a7","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e54","characters":62,"md":"The `fmjl fill` command rewrites any `md` into canonical form."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e58","hash":"552bd7e4665f8920","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":24,"md":"## 9. The Authoring Form"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e59","hash":"2abff29839cbb3dc","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e58","characters":132,"md":"The authoring form is a normal Markdown file that anyone can read and write. The tool turns each block of Markdown into one element."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e60","hash":"ff234de1bbd2fc60","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e58","characters":20,"md":"### 9.1 Front Matter"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e61","hash":"bd1b31a0094ef18d","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e60","characters":103,"md":"The file can start with front matter between two `---` lines. It holds the header fields, one per line:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e62","hash":"3d6986a06afa1ef2","type":"code","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e60","characters":125,"md":"```markdown\n---\ndoc: photosynthesis\ntitle: Photosynthesis Notes\nauthors: Riya Das, Amit Roy\ndate: 2026-09-26\nlang: en\n---\n```"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e63","hash":"6d7b1667c1abdd26","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e60","characters":48,"md":"Missing header fields are filled in by the tool."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e64","hash":"10811a67ef052034","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e58","characters":30,"md":"### 9.2 Blocks Become Elements"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e65","hash":"c3e8e1432b912be0","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e64","characters":53,"md":"The tool recognizes the type of each block by itself:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e66","hash":"f5d7b401b1aadbb6","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e64","characters":512,"md":"| You write | It becomes |\n| --- | --- |\n| `# Title`, `## Section` | `heading` |\n| Normal text | `paragraph` |\n| `- item` or `1. item` | `list` |\n| A Markdown table | `table` |\n| `<table>...</table>` | `table` with `html` |\n| A table cell holding only `^` or `<` | `table` with `html`: the cell is joined to the cell above (`^`) or to its left (`<`) |\n| `$$ ... $$` on its own | `formula` |\n| `![description](images/file.png)` on its own | `image` |\n| A fenced code block | `code` |\n| `> quoted text` | `quote` |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e115","hash":"f293405d04167656","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e64","characters":423,"md":"A table needs its separator row, `| --- | --- |`, and each row starts and ends with `|`. Lines that hold `|` but no separator row are read as a paragraph, and the tool warns. Joined cells must form a rectangle. To put a literal `^` or `<` alone in a cell, write `\\^` or `\\<`. When the tool writes the authoring form, a table whose `html` is in canonical form is shown with `^` and `<` again; other HTML is shown as written."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e67","hash":"c4a4bbb8fd91d714","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e58","characters":13,"md":"### 9.3 Notes"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e68","hash":"e92e8793be8e44e3","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e67","characters":175,"md":"A note is an HTML comment on its own line, directly before a block. Markdown viewers hide notes, so the document stays clean to read. A note adds fields to the block after it:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e69","hash":"28f112c6443eb3ad","type":"code","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e67","characters":88,"md":"```markdown\n<!-- type=caption reference=inputs -->\nTable 1: Inputs of photosynthesis\n```"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e70","hash":"bd13544d21c74f90","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e67","characters":16,"md":"A note can hold:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e71","hash":"7dfd8232521e4ce6","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e67","characters":367,"md":"1. The element's ID, such as `e7`, first.\n2. `type=` for types the tool cannot recognize by itself, such as `caption`, `footnote`, or `noise`.\n3. `subtype=`, `label=`, `page=`, `lang=`, `confidence=`, `parent=`, and `continues=`.\n4. Lists separated by commas: `pages=`, `bbox=`, `access=`, and `reference=`.\n5. `meta=` followed by JSON, always at the end of the note."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e72","hash":"6bc187ee27920f11","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e67","characters":295,"md":"References, `parent=`, and `continues=` can use an ID (`e7`), a label (`inputs`), or the words `above` and `below` for the block just before or just after this one; so a label cannot be named `above` or `below`. HTML comments that do not start like a note stay in the document as normal content."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e73","hash":"412658cb396b0d41","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e58","characters":14,"md":"### 9.4 Groups"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e74","hash":"7d3fc04f3e6f36b0","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e73","characters":279,"md":"A group starts with `<!-- group subtype=... -->`. The block right after that note is the group's title: it becomes the group's own `md` and is not an element of its own, so the group has one ID, the one in the group note. Every block until `<!-- /group -->` belongs to the group:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e75","hash":"381045cc9b388220","type":"code","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e73","characters":135,"md":"```markdown\n<!-- group subtype=figure -->\n**Figure 1: Inside a leaf**\n\n![Cross-section of a leaf](images/leaf.png)\n\n<!-- /group -->\n```"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e76","hash":"d16b77c3091bfe47","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e58","characters":36,"md":"### 9.5 Elements With Several Blocks"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e77","hash":"00a7f87968755b60","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e76","characters":168,"md":"When one element holds several blocks, such as an email with a blank line inside it, it starts with a note that has an ID or a label, and ends with a matching end note:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e78","hash":"38754d18c5210796","type":"code","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e76","characters":119,"md":"```markdown\n<!-- type=message label=hr-email -->\n**From:** HR\n\nPlease submit the form by Friday.\n<!-- /hr-email -->\n```"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e79","hash":"938a9b633662fd47","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e58","characters":36,"md":"### 9.6 Editing an Existing Document"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e80","hash":"42f7a6b8960cc19e","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e79","characters":204,"md":"1. Turn the storage form into the authoring form: `fmjl md name.fmjl`.\n2. Edit `name.md` in any editor. Each block keeps its ID in a small note, such as `<!-- e7 -->`.\n3. Turn it back: `fmjl new name.md`."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e81","hash":"16b02f091d84ea9c","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e79","characters":110,"md":"Blocks you did not change keep their IDs and hashes, new blocks get new IDs, and removed IDs are never reused."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e82","hash":"a9c8a0e7b69a565a","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":20,"md":"## 10. Input Formats"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e83","hash":"526957a8323cd8d3","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e82","characters":41,"md":"FMJL accepts all formats, in five groups:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e84","hash":"b5bba4a1e44b7ab9","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e82","characters":836,"md":"| Group | Formats | How they are converted |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Page-based | PDF, TIFF, PNG, JPG, and other scans | Full pipeline with OCR and layout detection; fills `page`, `bbox`, and `confidence` |\n| Structured | DOCX, DOC, PPTX, ODT, RTF, HTML, Markdown, EPUB, LaTeX | Structure is read directly, with no OCR; each slide becomes a `group` with subtype `slide` |\n| Tables | XLSX, XLS, ODS, CSV, TSV | Each sheet becomes a `group` with subtype `sheet`, holding `table` parts; CSV rows become `record` elements |\n| Code and data | Source code, JSON, JSONL, YAML, XML | Code becomes one `code` element per function or class; data becomes one `record` per object |\n| Email and transcripts | EML, MSG, MBOX, chat exports, SRT, VTT | One `message` per message, inside a `group` with subtype `thread`; one `utterance` per speaker turn |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e85","hash":"7a7d2f02312e4ddf","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e82","characters":80,"md":"Images saved by FMJL use PNG, WebP, JPG, or SVG. TIFF is accepted as input only."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e116","hash":"701fe81df8b5e6d3","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e82","characters":23,"md":"### 10.1 Importer Rules"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e117","hash":"fb0dea223ab92551","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e116","characters":117,"md":"Tools that convert other formats into FMJL follow these rules, so that two importers give the same shape of document:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e118","hash":"bdb247e088c12a92","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e116","characters":1936,"md":"1. Merged cells: a table with merged cells gets `html` in canonical form (section 8), never a Markdown table with empty cells.\n2. Figures: an image and its caption are two elements, the caption pointing to the image with `reference`. A `group` with subtype `figure` is used only when a figure holds several images.\n3. Captions: a caption that starts with \"Table\" belongs to the nearest table; one that starts with \"Figure\", \"Chart\", \"Diagram\", \"Image\" or \"Photo\" belongs to the nearest image. Only when no such neighbour exists may the other kind be linked. In Word files a table's caption usually sits above the table and a figure's caption below the figure.\n4. Heading levels: a heading is at most one level deeper than the heading before it; deeper ones are raised, so a document never jumps from level 2 to level 4.\n5. Charts drawn with lines and shapes (vector graphics) are rendered to a PNG image with subtype `diagram`, or `chart` when the caption calls it a chart, graph, or plot. Their axis labels belong to the image, not to the text.\n6. Formulas: Word math (OMML) is converted to LaTeX, display math as a `formula` element and inline math as `$...$`. A formula that cannot be recovered as LaTeX, which is the case in most PDFs, stays as the text that was read, inside its paragraph.\n7. Pages from structured formats: DOCX and similar files give `page` only from the page breaks the file remembers, and never `bbox`. Those numbers can be stale; only page-based formats give reliable positions.\n8. Tracked changes: an importer takes the accepted text, keeping insertions and dropping deletions. It warns, and records the counts in the header `meta` as `fmjl.tracked_changes`.\n9. Scans and OCR: when font sizes are unreliable, short lines in capital letters or with a section number, such as \"2.1 Methods\", become headings.\n10. Footnotes: written as in section 7.5, one `footnote` element right after the element that cites it."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e86","hash":"e50a2ac0710abc90","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":23,"md":"## 11. Processing Order"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e87","hash":"df3aa34efa90712f","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e86","characters":378,"md":"1. Quick check: confirm the file is valid, not a duplicate (`sha256`), which pages are digital or scanned, the language, and the page count.\n2. Convert: extract every part into elements and write the storage form.\n3. Final check: run the checks listed below.\n4. Chunk: build chunks as described in section 12.1.\n5. Embed: create embeddings and store them in the vector database."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e88","hash":"5dd122c5586ffa1b","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e86","characters":77,"md":"If the final check fails, convert again with a stronger tool and check again."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e89","hash":"179b7dd3157ca05a","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e86","characters":222,"md":"Large elements: a table longer than a converter's limit is split into parts, each repeating the header rows, linked with `continues`. A paragraph or list longer than one chunk is split at sentence boundaries when chunking."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e90","hash":"db3a1c1abdef5bc4","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e86","characters":30,"md":"The final check confirms that:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e91","hash":"0d32dc5eb6ba4b81","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e86","characters":437,"md":"1. Every line passes the JSON Schema in section 14.\n2. `elements` in the header is a number and equals the number of element lines.\n3. IDs and labels are unique, and no ID number is higher than `last_id`.\n4. Every `parent`, `reference`, `continues`, and in-document link points to an existing element.\n5. Every `file` exists in the `images/` folder.\n6. Every `md` is in canonical form, and every `hash` and `characters` value matches it."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e92","hash":"75815421fdd5e286","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":16,"md":"## 12. Retrieval"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e93","hash":"271dfa126a1ae59d","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e92","characters":119,"md":"One rule is required: always filter by `access` before searching, so users never see parts they are not allowed to see."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e119","hash":"00693d7cb7a197c2","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e92","characters":15,"md":"### 12.1 Chunks"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e120","hash":"ee416864af85f6d8","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e119","characters":100,"md":"A chunk is what a retriever embeds and returns. The `fmjl chunks` command builds chunks in two ways:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e121","hash":"ad2f0b9617cba457","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e119","characters":533,"md":"1. By element, the default: one chunk per element. A `caption` or `footnote` whose `reference` is a single element joins that element's chunk instead of forming its own. `noise`, `toc`, and `redaction` elements are never chunked.\n2. By section: one chunk per heading, holding the heading and every element below it up to the next heading. A heading with nothing under it but a deeper heading joins that heading's section. A section longer than a chosen number of characters is split into parts with the ids `id/1`, `id/2`, and so on."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e122","hash":"86703be2258a3c5b","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e119","characters":20,"md":"Every chunk carries:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e123","hash":"c6865176a2df7589","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e119","characters":756,"md":"1. `id`: the ID of its first element, plus `/n` for a split part. `elements`: the IDs it holds, when there are several.\n2. `text`: the titles of the headings and groups above the chunk joined with ` > `, a blank line, then the `md` of its elements joined with blank lines. This is the text to embed. `md` and `path` hold the two parts separately.\n3. `hash`: the element's `hash`, or for several elements the first 16 hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 of their hashes joined with newlines. A chunk needs a new embedding only when its `hash` changes.\n4. `doc`, `type`, `page` or `pages`, `bbox`, `file`, `reference`, `access`, `title`, and `source`, copied from the element and the header, so the retriever can filter, cite, and show the original region."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e124","hash":"1024bece68b5ce35","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e92","characters":30,"md":"### 12.2 Recommended Practices"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e94","hash":"28a6cbd2b79989fa","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e124","characters":72,"md":"The rest are recommendations. A system may change them for good reasons:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e95","hash":"dea367ffba5468f9","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e124","characters":508,"md":"1. Don't embed `noise`, `toc`, or `redaction` elements.\n2. Embed `md`, including for tables that also have `html`.\n3. Add each element's section path, rebuilt from its `parent` chain, to its chunk for context.\n4. Return `caption` and `citation` elements together with the elements they reference, and a chart together with its data table.\n5. When an answer uses content with low `confidence`, show the original region using `page` and `bbox`.\n6. Cite answers with the element `id` and the page number plus 1."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e96","hash":"0083089b79bccdfa","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":19,"md":"## 13. Reader Rules"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e97","hash":"4c522f98ba75ce75","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e96","characters":252,"md":"1. Readers ignore fields they do not know, so newer files stay readable.\n2. Readers treat unknown types as `paragraph`.\n3. A reader for version 0.x can read any file of version 0.x. The `fmjl upgrade` command turns older files into the current version."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e98","hash":"1231327387a1ca3e","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":18,"md":"## 14. JSON Schema"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e99","hash":"28b4038756f1ec44","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e98","characters":225,"md":"This schema checks every line of the storage form automatically (JSON Schema draft 2020-12). A line is valid if it matches either the header or the element definition. Checks that need the whole file are listed in section 11."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e100","hash":"7b5ee4aba59e6cc3","type":"code","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e98","characters":9677,"md":"```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"title\": \"FMJL line, version 0.5\",\n  \"oneOf\": [\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/header\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/element\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"header\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\n        \"type\",\n        \"version\",\n        \"doc\",\n        \"source\",\n        \"sha256\",\n        \"protection\",\n        \"signed\",\n        \"converter\",\n        \"structure\",\n        \"elements\",\n        \"created\",\n        \"lang\",\n        \"access\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"type\": {\n          \"const\": \"document\"\n        },\n        \"version\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+$\"\n        },\n        \"doc\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+$\"\n        },\n        \"source\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"sha256\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\"\n        },\n        \"protection\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"none\",\n            \"password\",\n            \"certificate\",\n            \"drm\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"signed\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"converter\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"minLength\": 1\n        },\n        \"structure\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"elements\": {\n          \"type\": [\n            \"integer\",\n            \"null\"\n          ],\n          \"minimum\": 0\n        },\n        \"created\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"format\": \"date-time\"\n        },\n        \"lang\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z]{2,3}(-[A-Za-z0-9]+)*$\"\n        },\n        \"access\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z0-9_.:-]+$\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"title\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"authors\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"date\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9]{4}(-[0-9]{2}(-[0-9]{2})?)?$\"\n        },\n        \"summary\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"last_id\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 0\n        },\n        \"meta\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"element\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\n        \"id\",\n        \"hash\",\n        \"type\",\n        \"parent\",\n        \"characters\",\n        \"md\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+#e[1-9][0-9]*$\"\n        },\n        \"hash\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{16}$\"\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"heading\",\n            \"paragraph\",\n            \"list\",\n            \"table\",\n            \"formula\",\n            \"code\",\n            \"image\",\n            \"caption\",\n            \"footnote\",\n            \"form_field\",\n            \"annotation\",\n            \"redaction\",\n            \"noise\",\n            \"message\",\n            \"utterance\",\n            \"record\",\n            \"citation\",\n            \"quote\",\n            \"toc\",\n            \"group\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"subtype\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"label\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*$\"\n        },\n        \"level\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 6\n        },\n        \"parent\": {\n          \"type\": [\n            \"string\",\n            \"null\"\n          ],\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+#e[1-9][0-9]*$\"\n        },\n        \"page\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 0\n        },\n        \"pages\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 2,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 0\n          }\n        },\n        \"bbox\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 4,\n          \"maxItems\": 4,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 0,\n            \"maximum\": 1000\n          }\n        },\n        \"characters\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 0\n        },\n        \"reference\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+#e[1-9][0-9]*$\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"array\",\n              \"minItems\": 2,\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\",\n                \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+#e[1-9][0-9]*$\"\n              }\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"continues\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z0-9_-]+#e[1-9][0-9]*$\"\n        },\n        \"confidence\": {\n          \"type\": \"number\",\n          \"minimum\": 0,\n          \"maximum\": 1\n        },\n        \"lang\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[a-z]{2,3}(-[A-Za-z0-9]+)*$\"\n        },\n        \"access\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z0-9_.:-]+$\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"html\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"latex\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^images/[^/]+\\\\.(png|webp|jpg|jpeg|svg)$\"\n        },\n        \"meta\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        },\n        \"md\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"dependentRequired\": {\n        \"bbox\": [\n          \"page\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"not\": {\n        \"required\": [\n          \"page\",\n          \"pages\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"allOf\": [\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"heading\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"level\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"formula\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"latex\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"image\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"file\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"subtype\": {\n                \"enum\": [\n                  \"logo\",\n                  \"stamp\",\n                  \"signature\",\n                  \"chart\",\n                  \"diagram\",\n                  \"photo\",\n                  \"qr_code\",\n                  \"barcode\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"noise\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"subtype\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"subtype\": {\n                \"enum\": [\n                  \"header\",\n                  \"footer\",\n                  \"watermark\",\n                  \"page_number\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"group\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"subtype\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"subtype\": {\n                \"enum\": [\n                  \"slide\",\n                  \"sidebar\",\n                  \"figure\",\n                  \"box\",\n                  \"sheet\",\n                  \"thread\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"level\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"heading\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"html\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"table\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"latex\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"formula\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"file\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"const\": \"image\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"if\": {\n            \"required\": [\n              \"subtype\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"then\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"enum\": [\n                  \"image\",\n                  \"noise\",\n                  \"group\"\n                ]\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e101","hash":"59fd09f2f4f18b10","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":15,"md":"## 15. Examples"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e102","hash":"61784c0edc297db0","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e101","characters":45,"md":"A short leave policy PDF in the storage form:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e103","hash":"103522706d11b0bf","type":"code","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e101","characters":1713,"md":"```json\n{\"type\":\"document\",\"version\":\"0.5\",\"doc\":\"leave_policy\",\"source\":\"leave_policy.pdf\",\"sha256\":\"af179a761f988e6a40d5154b3c3ce735ba94d23ebd82d8e24e3d80de4e2dda68\",\"protection\":\"none\",\"signed\":false,\"converter\":\"docling 2.x\",\"structure\":true,\"elements\":6,\"created\":\"2026-09-26T10:30:00Z\",\"lang\":\"en\",\"access\":[\"all\"],\"title\":\"Leave Policy\",\"last_id\":6}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"hash\":\"b323ab53d73b48e7\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"level\":1,\"parent\":null,\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[80,60,620,95],\"characters\":14,\"md\":\"# Leave Policy\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e2\",\"hash\":\"b91ad9f6b39e617a\",\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[80,110,920,170],\"characters\":105,\"md\":\"This policy applies to all full-time employees from their first day of work. See [Table 1](#leave-types).\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e3\",\"hash\":\"79e15a433bf84d1c\",\"type\":\"table\",\"label\":\"leave-types\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[80,190,700,330],\"characters\":89,\"md\":\"| Leave type | Days per year |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Sick leave | 12 |\\n| Paternity leave | 15 |\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e4\",\"hash\":\"fd6cd4502fca6a4a\",\"type\":\"caption\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[80,335,400,355],\"characters\":20,\"reference\":\"leave_policy#e3\",\"md\":\"Table 1: Leave types\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e5\",\"hash\":\"8f843b2362f0d607\",\"type\":\"image\",\"subtype\":\"stamp\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[700,820,900,940],\"characters\":66,\"confidence\":0.91,\"file\":\"images/leave_policy_e5.png\",\"md\":\"Round blue stamp reading \\\"Brightpath Technologies, HR Department\\\".\"}\n{\"id\":\"leave_policy#e6\",\"hash\":\"731af9f7a14feaf5\",\"type\":\"noise\",\"subtype\":\"footer\",\"parent\":\"leave_policy#e1\",\"page\":0,\"bbox\":[460,960,540,980],\"characters\":6,\"md\":\"Page 1\"}\n```"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e104","hash":"3a7889b77d0068fd","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e101","characters":40,"md":"The same document in the authoring form:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e105","hash":"e9228f8e92c6808a","type":"code","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e101","characters":842,"md":"```markdown\n---\nfmjl: \"0.5\"\ndoc: leave_policy\ntitle: Leave Policy\nlang: en\naccess: [\"all\"]\nsource: leave_policy.pdf\nprotection: none\nsigned: false\nlast_id: 6\n---\n\n<!-- e1 page=0 bbox=80,60,620,95 -->\n# Leave Policy\n\n<!-- e2 page=0 bbox=80,110,920,170 -->\nThis policy applies to all full-time employees from their first day of work. See [Table 1](#leave-types).\n\n<!-- e3 label=leave-types page=0 bbox=80,190,700,330 -->\n| Leave type | Days per year |\n| --- | --- |\n| Sick leave | 12 |\n| Paternity leave | 15 |\n\n<!-- e4 type=caption page=0 bbox=80,335,400,355 reference=e3 -->\nTable 1: Leave types\n\n<!-- e5 subtype=stamp page=0 bbox=700,820,900,940 confidence=0.91 -->\n![Round blue stamp reading \"Brightpath Technologies, HR Department\".](images/leave_policy_e5.png)\n\n<!-- e6 type=noise subtype=footer page=0 bbox=460,960,540,980 -->\nPage 1\n```"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e106","hash":"9e61ca8a82937604","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":12,"md":"## 16. Tools"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e107","hash":"876d7bcf45eea157","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e106","characters":131,"md":"The reference tool is the Python package `fmjl` (`pip install fmjl`, or `python -m fmjl` from the repository). It has ten commands:"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e108","hash":"4c88c574424178b6","type":"table","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e106","characters":899,"md":"| Command | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `fmjl new notes.md` | Turns the authoring form into the storage form, `notes.fmjl` |\n| `fmjl md notes.fmjl` | Turns the storage form into the authoring form, `notes.md` |\n| `fmjl fill notes.fmjl` | Fills in `id`, `hash`, `characters`, and `parent`, and makes `md` canonical |\n| `fmjl check notes.fmjl` | Checks every rule and prints errors with line numbers |\n| `fmjl view notes.fmjl` | Prints the document as clean Markdown, without notes |\n| `fmjl info notes.fmjl` | Prints the title, element counts, and an outline |\n| `fmjl upgrade old.fmjl` | Turns a version 0.1 to 0.4 file into version 0.5 |\n| `fmjl pdf report.pdf` | Turns a PDF into both forms and an `images/` folder |\n| `fmjl docx report.docx` | Turns a Word file into both forms and an `images/` folder |\n| `fmjl chunks notes.fmjl` | Prints retriever-ready chunks (section 12.1) as JSON Lines |"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e109","hash":"bc2741e68c8d14db","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e106","characters":404,"md":"It needs Python and one package, `pip install jsonschema`; the PDF importer also needs `pip install pymupdf`. From Python, `import fmjl` gives `load`, `save`, `chunks`, `changed_chunks`, and `check`. The VS Code extension `rupakkumar.fmjl` converts between both forms without Python and checks every rule while typing. Tools in other languages are welcome; they follow this rulebook, not the Python tool."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e110","hash":"3305c158a9bcfcb5","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":22,"md":"## 17. Version History"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e111","hash":"4fb7c190cd27947c","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e110","characters":1164,"md":"1. Version 0.1: first draft, with the extension `.jsonl`.\n2. Version 0.2: the extension `.fmjl` and the `fmjl` tool.\n3. Version 0.3: the authoring form; canonical Markdown; IDs that never change; labels; the `group` type; `continues`; `meta`; header fields `title`, `authors`, `date`, `summary`, and `last_id`; `elements` may be `null` while writing; JPG and SVG images; retrieval rules become recommendations; the rulebook becomes the authority over the tool.\n4. Version 0.4: the format is named FMJL, short for Format, Markdown, JSON Lines; the placeholder name \"Format X\" is retired; the license is MIT. No rules changed, so 0.3 files stay valid.\n5. Version 0.5: merged cells can be written in a Markdown table with `^` and `<`, and tool-written HTML has one canonical form (sections 8 and 9.2); `above` and `below` in notes (9.3); the group title explained (9.4); the `md` form of footnotes (7.5); `fmjl.` names reserved in `meta` (7.6); importer rules (10.1); chunks defined (12.1); the tool warns about a table typed without its separator row; the `pdf`, `docx`, and `chunks` commands. No 0.4 file becomes invalid, so `fmjl upgrade` only changes the version."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e112","hash":"835d5475271526f8","type":"paragraph","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e110","characters":159,"md":"Moving from 0.2 to 0.3: run `fmjl upgrade`. Some `md` texts change once into canonical form, so their hashes change and those elements are embedded again once."}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e113","hash":"1960efb46acfd76f","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e1","characters":22,"md":"## 18. Not Decided Yet"}
{"id":"fmjl_rulebook#e114","hash":"89b4f97f60f66ea7","type":"list","parent":"fmjl_rulebook#e113","characters":451,"md":"1. Version 1.0 will be released after the accuracy benchmark. From 1.0 on, every 1.x reader will read every 1.x file.\n2. Recovering LaTeX from formulas in PDF files, where only the drawn characters are available.\n3. Reading order for pages with three or more columns or with sidebars; the importer handles two columns.\n4. OCR for scanned pages: the path exists and needs Tesseract, but its `confidence` values have not been checked against real scans."}
